<h2>4. Data Preprocessing & Cleaning Pipeline</h2>

  <h3>1. Null Value Imputation</h3>
  <p>Evaluated missing data percentage across all features. Sensor dropout in PM2.5 (2.3%) and NO2 (1.8%) imputed using time-weighted linear interpolation, preserving seasonal continuity.</p>
  <div class="code-block">df['pm25']&nbsp;=&nbsp;df['pm25'].interpolate(method='time')<br>df['no2'].fillna(df.groupby('city_zone')['no2'].transform('median'),&nbsp;inplace=True)</div>

  <h3>2. Outlier Detection & IQR Treatment</h3>
  <p>Applied Interquartile Range (IQR) technique on SO2 and PM10 to distinguish valid catastrophic industrial release spikes from sensor calibration errors. Values outside 1.5 * IQR were windsorized.</p>
  <div class="code-block">Q1&nbsp;=&nbsp;df['pm10'].quantile(0.25)<br>Q3&nbsp;=&nbsp;df['pm10'].quantile(0.75)<br>IQR&nbsp;=&nbsp;Q3&nbsp;-&nbsp;Q1<br>lower_bound&nbsp;=&nbsp;Q1&nbsp;-&nbsp;1.5&nbsp;*&nbsp;IQR<br>upper_bound&nbsp;=&nbsp;Q3&nbsp;+&nbsp;1.5&nbsp;*&nbsp;IQR<br>df['pm10']&nbsp;=&nbsp;df['pm10'].clip(lower_bound,&nbsp;upper_bound)</div>

  <h3>3. Feature Engineering & Temporal Extraction</h3>
  <p>Extracted Month, DayOfWeek, and Weekend indicators. Computed a composite PM2.5/PM10 ratio indicating combustion vs dust prevalence. Standardized numerical columns using StandardScaler.</p>
  <div class="code-block">df['pm_ratio']&nbsp;=&nbsp;df['pm25']&nbsp;/&nbsp;(df['pm10']&nbsp;+&nbsp;1e-5)<br>df['is_weekend']&nbsp;=&nbsp;pd.to_datetime(df['date']).dt.dayofweek.isin([5,&nbsp;6]).astype(int)<br>scaler&nbsp;=&nbsp;StandardScaler()<br>X_scaled&nbsp;=&nbsp;scaler.fit_transform(df[numerical_cols])</div>


<h2>5. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) Insights</h2>

  <div style="border-left: 3pt solid #3b82f6; padding-left: 8pt; margin: 10pt 0;">
    <strong>PM2.5 vs Respiratory Admissions Strong Linear Coupling</strong> [r = 0.842 Correlation]<br>
    <em>Visual Tool: Scatter Plot with OLS Trend Line</em><br>
    Pearson correlation analysis reveals a decisive r = 0.842 (p < 0.001) between 24-hour average PM2.5 exposure and acute respiratory emergency admissions.
  </div>

  <div style="border-left: 3pt solid #3b82f6; padding-left: 8pt; margin: 10pt 0;">
    <strong>Industrial Corridor Exceeds WHO Limits on 78% of Days</strong> [78% Days Non-Compliant]<br>
    <em>Visual Tool: Zonal Box Plot & Violin Plot</em><br>
    The Industrial Corridor recorded median PM2.5 of 92.4 µg/m³, which is over 6x the WHO 24-hour guideline of 15 µg/m³, demonstrating deep spatial disparity.
  </div>

  <div style="border-left: 3pt solid #3b82f6; padding-left: 8pt; margin: 10pt 0;">
    <strong>Thermal Inversion Amplifies Winter Contaminants</strong> [+44% Winter Spike]<br>
    <em>Visual Tool: Multi-line Temporal Trend Chart</em><br>
    During winter months with temperatures < 18°C and low wind speed, ground-level pollutant accumulation rose by 44% compared to summer baselines due to atmospheric trapping.
  </div>

  <div style="border-left: 3pt solid #3b82f6; padding-left: 8pt; margin: 10pt 0;">
    <strong>Weekend Effect: Vehicle NO2 Drops by 31%</strong> [-31.2% Weekend NO2]<br>
    <em>Visual Tool: Grouped Bar Comparison Chart</em><br>
    NO2 levels plummeted by 31.2% on Saturdays and Sundays in Downtown Commercial sectors, confirming traffic congestion as the primary urban NO2 driver.
  </div>


<h2>6. Machine Learning Model & Evaluation</h2>
<p><strong>Primary Algorithm:</strong> Random Forest Classifier with Hyperparameter Tuning (GridSearchCV)</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Evaluation Metric</th>
      <th>Baseline (Logistic Regression)</th>
      <th>Final Tuned Model (Random Forest)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Accuracy</strong></td>
      <td>81.4%</td>
      <td><strong>93.8%</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Precision</strong></td>
      <td>78.2%</td>
      <td><strong>94.2%</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Recall</strong></td>
      <td>75.6%</td>
      <td><strong>93.1%</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>F1-Score</strong></td>
      <td>76.8%</td>
      <td><strong>93.6%</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>ROC-AUC Score</strong></td>
      <td>0.824</td>
